OpenOCD (Open On-Chip Debugger) provides JTAG/SWD debugging and
in-system programming for embedded targets, with GDB server, telnet
and Tcl interfaces.

This is the Raspberry Pi downstream fork of OpenOCD.  Compared to
devel/openocd it adds support for Pico-series devices (RP2040 and
RP2350), the picoprobe and Raspberry Pi Debug Probe adapters, CMSIS-DAP
multi-DAP, and other Raspberry Pi specific enhancements.

The program is installed as "openocd-rpi" and data files are installed
under share/openocd-rpi, so this package can be installed alongside
devel/openocd.
